Translation patch: `BinlogValue`: out-of-scope decoders and string rendering

Change: In `BinlogValue::into_owned` and `MyDeserialize for BinlogValue`: the JSON-diff conversion `x.into_iter().map(|x| x.into_owned()).collect()` moves into `jsondiff::json_diffs_into_owned`; the partial-JSON loop into `jsondiff::parse_json_diffs`; `json_value_buf.parse(())` (JSONB) into `jsonb::parse_jsonb_value`; `Decimal::read_bin(..)` + `to_string().into_bytes()` into `decimal::read_bin_to_string_bytes`; `(1900 + y).to_string().into_bytes()` and `sec.to_string().into_bytes()` become `trusted::string_into_bytes(trusted::i128_to_string(x as i128))` (the existing helpers of patch 40); `format!("{}.{:06}", sec, usec).into_bytes()` moves into `binlog::trusted::timestamp2_frac_bytes`; `bytes.into()` (`&[u8]` to `Vec<u8>`) becomes `bytes.to_vec()`; `ColumnType::try_from(b).unwrap_or(t)` becomes a `match`. The new helpers in `jsonb`, `jsondiff`, `decimal` (modules opaque in the translation) and `binlog::trusted` are the moved code verbatim.
Why: JSONB, JSON diffs and decimals are out of scope (opaque modules); `to_string`, `format!` and `From<&[T]> for Vec<T>` are not modelled (patch 58); closures and the loop with `?`: see patch 143.
Behaviour: Identical: the helpers contain exactly the moved expressions; an `i32` renders the same as the `i128` it widens to; `to_vec` is std's `From<&[T]>`; the `match` is `unwrap_or`.

